  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal obligations for NAICS 541618 are $251M year to date and spread across 658 awards. Average award size for the industry is $382K. Obligations fell 70.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows variation with $537M in FY21, $913M in FY22, $864M in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $843M in FY25. Federal buyers concentrate spending: the Department of Health and Human Services leads with $116M, and the Department of Defense follows with $53.9M. Vendors capture a range of award sizes with NATIONAL COLLEGIATE INVENTORS & INNOVATORS ALLIANCE, INC. receiving $68M and ISLAND PEER REVIEW ORGANIZATION INC receiving $52.4M. This mix of agencies and prime contractors indicates demand is currently lower than last year but still meaningful for contractors that align to the top buyers and named vendors.",
